When `hci_register_dev()` fails, the `HCI_UART_PROTO_INIT` flag remains set (it was set earlier by `set_bit(HCI_UART_PROTO_INIT, &hu->flags)`). This allows `hci_uart_tty_receive()` to enter the protocol-specific receive handler even after `hu->proto->close(hu)` has been called and `hu->hdev` set to NULL, leading to a null pointer dereference or use-after-free.

